<content contentuid="he6d200bcg966252fdg29235da3g5b3d916e" version="1">UTAC COMBAT CONTROL</content>
<content contentuid="h9f8e7d6cg5c4bg4a3bg9b8ag7f6e5d4c3b2a" version="1">Release AI Control</content>
<content contentuid="h1a2b3c4dge5f6g4a1bg8c9dga5b4c3d2e1f0" version="1">Removes AI control from the target, returning them to player control.</content>
<content contentuid="ha1b2c3d4ge5f6g7a8bg9c0dge1f2a3b4c5d6" version="1">UTAC Orders</content>
<content contentuid="hb2c3d4e5gf6a7g8b9cg0d1eg2f3a4b5c6d7e8" version="1">Issue global tactical orders to your AI companions. Focus or ignore specific targets.</content>
<content contentuid="h1f2a3b4cg5d6eg7f8ag9b0cgd1e2f3a4b5c6" version="1">Focus Target</content>
<content contentuid="h2a3b4c5dg6e7fg8a9bg0c1dge2f3a4b5c6d7" version="1">All UTAC-controlled allies will prioritize attacking this enemy.</content>
<content contentuid="h3b4c5d6eg7f8ag9b0cg1d2eg3f4a5b6c7d8" version="1">Ignore Target</content>
<content contentuid="h4c5d6e7fg8a9bg0c1dg2e3fg4a5b6c7d8e9" version="1">All UTAC-controlled allies will avoid targeting this enemy.</content>
<content contentuid="h5a6b7c8dge9f0g1a2bg3c4dg5e6f7a8b9c0d1" version="1">NPC Mode</content>
<content contentuid="h6b7c8d9eg0f1ag2b3cg4d5eg6f7a8b9c0d1e2" version="1">When active, this companion becomes an NPC ally in combat (green circle). Improves AI spell usage and self-targeting.</content>
<content contentuid="hmcm7fac0005shadowname000000000005" version="1">Protect AI from Shadow Curse</content>
<content contentuid="hmcm7fac0006shadowdesc000000000006" version="1">Optional hidden safety net for UTAC-controlled allies and summons in Act 2. Grants shadow-curse immunity so AI pathing cannot strand them outside safe light.</content>
<content contentuid="hmcm7fac0001coredesc00000000000001" version="1">Master toggles. In co-op, only the host's MCM settings apply.</content>
<content contentuid="hmcm7fac0002presetname00000000000002" version="1">Archetype preset</content>
<content contentuid="hmcm7fac0003presetdesc00000000000003" version="1">0 = Default, 1 = Defensive Healer, 2 = Proactive Healer, 3 = Battle Cleric. Takes effect immediately when changed.</content>
<content contentuid="hmcm7fac0004customresdesc000000000004" version="1">Comma- or semicolon-separated resource names for custom spell pools (e.g. from other mods).</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000001" version="1">UTAC</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000002" version="1">Core</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000003" version="1">Core Settings</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000004" version="1">Enable UTAC</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000005" version="1">Master toggle for the entire mod.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000006" version="1">Auto-Apply AI to Summons</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000007" version="1">Automatically apply UTAC Summon AI to friendly summons when they are created or enter combat.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000008" version="1">AI Assistance</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000009" version="1">Strong Archetype Assistance</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000000a" version="1">Enable archetype mechanical buffs</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000000b" version="1">Optional mechanical buffs themed by archetype. These are not required for AI control and are off by default.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000000c" version="1">Assistance Toggles</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000000d" version="1">Enable light combat assistance</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000000e" version="1">Allow short-lived, light combat assistance. This can grant real stats, so it is off by default.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000000f" version="1">Enable movement and safety assistance</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000010" version="1">Allow movement and surface-escape helpers. Trap awareness remains part of core AI control.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000011" version="1">Enable resource/action assistance</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000012" version="1">Allow UTAC to encourage spell slots, abilities, and consumables. Can grant limited action economy; off by default.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000013" version="1">Action Blocks</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000014" version="1">Block Dash for UTAC allies</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000015" version="1">When enabled, UTAC-controlled allies will avoid using Dash unless explicitly ordered.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000016" version="1">Block Throw actions for UTAC allies</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000017" version="1">Blocks common Throw, Improvised Weapon, and Frenzied Throw actions for UTAC-controlled allies in combat. Useful if NPC Mode causes unsafe thrown items, but does not cover every story or modded throw spell.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000018" version="1">Block Shove for UTAC allies</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000019" version="1">When enabled, UTAC-controlled allies will avoid using Shove. Off by default because this overrides the vanilla Shove spell for UTAC allies.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000001a" version="1">Soft Resource Tuning</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000001b" version="1">Prefer conserving high slots</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000001c" version="1">Soft behavior hint used by resource helpers. It only prevents UTAC from encouraging high-slot spending when pressure is low; it does not block spells.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000001d" version="1">Soft high slot level</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000001e" version="1">Spell slots at or above this level are treated as high-value by the soft resource-helper logic.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000001f" version="1">Soft spend pressure</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000020" version="1">Minimum nearby enemies before UTAC may encourage high-slot spending in non-urgent situations.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000021" version="1">Action Surge: HP% threshold</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000022" version="1">Bruiser companions will be encouraged to use Action Surge when HP drops below this percent.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000023" version="1">Emergency spell slot restoration chance (%)</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000024" version="1">Optional chance per turn that a caster archetype regains a level 1 spell slot under pressure. Default is 0 because this is real resource assistance.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000025" version="1">Additional Spell Resources</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000026" version="1">Healer</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000027" version="1">Healer AI Settings</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000028" version="1">HP% threshold for urgent triage</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000029" version="1">At or below this HP%, the healer prioritizes healing/revive and allies are counted as 'low HP' for AI decisions.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000002a" version="1">Debug</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000002b" version="1">Debug Settings</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000002c" version="1">Enable Debug Logging</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000002d" version="1">Show detailed AI decision logs in console.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000002e" version="1">Enable enhanced archetype buffs (experimental)</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000002f" version="1">Debug-tier mechanical assistance for Bruisers and Spellcasters. Very powerful and not part of normal AI control.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000030" version="1">AI Sculpt Spells Safety</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000031" version="1">Grants AI-controlled characters a hidden Sculpt Spells helper so many Evocation area spells avoid harming allies. Disabled by default because it changes combat balance and does not cover every spell.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000032" version="1">Use editable spell block list</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000033" version="1">Enables the editable blocked-spell list below. Add, remove, or disable spell IDs there to control which utility spells UTAC AI should avoid in combat.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000034" version="1">Edit blocked utility spell IDs</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000035" version="1">Typed spell IDs blocked for UTAC-controlled AI while spell policy is enabled. Only enabled rows are blocked; extra known utility candidates are included disabled by default.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000036" version="1">Block high spell slots in low-pressure combat</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000037" version="1">Hard limiter. Temporarily blocks higher normal spell slots for caster AI during low-pressure combat. Default off.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000038" version="1">Hard block from spell-slot level</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000039" version="1">Normal spell slots at this level and higher are blocked while the hard limiter is active.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000003a" version="1">Disable limiter when enemies nearby</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000003b" version="1">If this many enemies are nearby, high spell slots are allowed again. Set to 0 to always allow high slots during combat.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000003c" version="1">Spells &amp; Resources</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000003d" version="1">Spell Policy</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000003e" version="1">Spell Slot Limiter</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g00000000003f" version="1">Resource Helpers</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000040" version="1">Summon auto-apply exclusions</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000041" version="1">Advanced: editable root/template UUID list for summons UTAC should not auto-control. Use this for utility summons such as Pack Rats. Runtime spawned character UUIDs usually change and should not be used. Manual archetype assignment still works.</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000042" version="1">Block Jump for UTAC allies</content>
<content contentuid="h7fac0100g0000g4000g8000g000000000043" version="1">Blocks normal AI Jump for UTAC-controlled allies in combat. Useful if companions make unsafe vertical jumps, but may reduce mobility or pathing options.</content>
</contentList>
